# Normalise line endings.
#
# The repository stores LF and checks out LF on every platform, regardless of a
# contributor's core.autocrlf setting. This is not cosmetic: `index.js` is the
# package's bin entry, and a shebang terminated by CRLF makes Linux and macOS
# look for an interpreter literally named "node\r". That breaks
# `npx <package>` with "env: node\r: No such file or directory" — while working
# fine on the Windows machine that published it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures must never be line-ending normalised; objects-sample.inv is a
# real zlib-compressed Sphinx inventory and any rewriting corrupts it.
*.inv binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
